Description: personal curated "awesome list" checked against Software Heritage
 awesome-personal-list is a small personal tool for curating a list of
 upstream projects. Entries are flat JSON files on disk (no database),
 written in C on top of the ecewo web framework.
 .
 Includes a companion awesome-personal-list-checker binary, meant to be run
 periodically (see the bundled systemd timer), which re-verifies every
 curated source against the Software Heritage archive.
 .
 Listens on 127.0.0.1:48889 by default; put a reverse proxy such as nginx
 in front for TLS and public exposure.
